# This is `bat`s configuration file. Each line either contains a comment or a command-line option that you want to pass to `bat` by default. You can run `bat --help` to get a list of all possible configuration options.

# Highlighting theme. With no --theme set, bat >= 0.25 detects the terminal's
# background and picks --theme-dark / --theme-light on its own, so bat follows
# wezterm — and therefore the Windows app theme — like neovim does.
# Run `bat --list-themes` for a list of all available themes.
--theme-dark="achroma"
--theme-light="achroma-light"

--style="numbers,changes,header"

# Enable this to use italic text on the terminal. This is not supported on all terminal emulators (like tmux, by default):
# --italic-text=always

# Uncomment the following line to disable automatic paging:
# --paging=never

# Uncomment the following line if you are using less version >= 551 and want to enable mouse scrolling support in `bat` when running inside tmux. This might disable text selection, unless you press shift.
# --pager="less --RAW-CONTROL-CHARS --quit-if-one-screen --mouse"

# Syntax mappings: map a certain filename pattern to a language. Example 1: use the C++ syntax for Arduino .ino files Example 2: Use ".gitignore"-style highlighting for ".ignore" files
# --map-syntax "\*.ino:C++"
# --map-syntax ".ignore:Git Ignore"
